# s86-m01: sprint build plans are CONTRACTS, and prettier silently corrupts them.
#
# These documents are dense technical prose full of glob patterns, dunder paths and
# regex fragments. Prettier's markdown emphasis normalization reads those as inline
# formatting and rewrites the characters: `__snapshots__` becomes `**snapshots**`,
# `console.*` becomes `console._`, `mutable_status:*` becomes `mutable_status:_`.
# Running `prettier --write` on cmos/planning/s86-say-only-what-you-know.md damaged
# 73 lines that way — including the path to the tool-definitions snapshot that four
# separate missions are ordered around. It is also NOT IDEMPOTENT here: --write
# followed by --check still fails, oscillating between two differently-corrupted
# states, so there is no "just format it once" resolution.
#
# A formatter that rewrites the content of a contract while reporting a style fix is
# precisely this sprint's defect class. Plans are read by humans and agents, never
# imported or rendered by the build, so nothing is lost by exempting them.
